t:
such as have several words in common; but which, by the addition of other words, convey an opposite, at least a different meaning. Such are those,

\[
\begin{align*}
&\text{Et canis} \quad \text{in silva venatur} \\
&\text{Inpsus nutritur} \quad \text{Omnia servat} \\
&\text{Concordia, a town of Italy, in the duchy of Mirandola; seated on the river Sechia, 5 miles west of Mirandola, and 15 miles south-east of Mantua; subject to the house of Austria. E. Long. 11. 22. N. Lat. 44. 52.}
\end{align*}
\]
